Adds chrome/renderer/phlink/adblock/cosmetic_filter_agent.{h,cc}
— a per-RenderFrame content::RenderFrameObserver that:

  * On DidCommitProvisionalLoad, requests
    phlink::mojom::AdblockCosmeticFilter via the frame's
    BrowserInterfaceBrokerProxy and asks for cosmetic resources
    keyed on the document URL.
  * On the reply, concatenates hide_selectors into a single
    'display: none' rule (with !important) and inserts it via
    blink::WebDocument::InsertStyleSheet.
  * Runs the optional injected_script (uBO-style +js scriptlet)
    via blink::WebLocalFrame::ExecuteScript on the main world.
  * Self-deletes on RenderFrame destruction.

Skips non-http(s) URLs to avoid round-trips for chrome:// and
devtools:// frames. Honors $generichide by dropping the bundle
on that frame (conservative: matches Brave's renderer behavior).

Wired into ChromeContentRendererClient::RenderFrameCreated next
to the prerender observer. chrome target builds green;
phlink_adblock_unittests 10/10 SUCCESS.

This closes the 5-05 cosmetic-filter slice end-to-end:
adblock-rust -> C++ Engine -> mojom -> CosmeticFilterHost
-> CosmeticFilterAgent -> WebDocument.

Refs PRD section 6.1, section 10.1 (engine never crosses into
the renderer process), plan 5-05c.
